  "query_preview": "..\nKey Message 1...Scattered showers and thunderstorms through tonight, \nfollowed by periodic chances for showers and storms through midweek, \nalthough plenty of dry time can be expected.\n\nArea of convection essentially tied to a MCV currently pushing east\nacross far northern Pennsylvania. This feature will exit the region\nby late this afternoon. Although there may be a pop up shower or\nstorm on the periphery of the MCV, mainly dry weather is expected\nthis afternoon. \n\nA cold front will push south across western and north-central New \nYork tonight. Moderate shear and a moist airmass will remain in \nplace within the warm sector ahead of the boundary, however loss of \ndaytime heating will result in less instability. The potential for \nsevere weather appears low, but scattered showers and storms will\nbe possible as the boundary pushes south through the region. \nPotential for localized heavy rainfall remains in place within \nthe moist airmass.\n\nThe cold front will stall just to our south tonight, then remain \nnearly stationary through midweek. Drier air will reside to the \nnorth of the boundary, with the main threat of showers and a few \nstorms toward the western Southern Tier Tuesday through Wednesday \ncloser to the frontal boundary, and mainly dry weather elsewhere.",
